{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ea7e39d99b57bc5aa5", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Rotational Motion - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f897"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f702", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cab"], "question": {"text": "The moment of inertia of a circular ring of mass $M$ and diameter r about a tangential axis lying in the plane of the ring is :"}, "options": [{"id": "016e4a", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{Mr}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69b"}, {"id": "70d51f", "text": "$\\frac{3}{8} \\mathrm{Mr}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69c"}, {"id": "7fab41", "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{Mr}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69d"}, {"id": "ebb278", "text": "$2 \\mathrm{Mr}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f69f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "A stationary horizontal disc is free to rotate about its axis. When a torque is applied on it, its kinetic energy as a function of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math>, where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math> is the angle by which it has rotated, is given as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If its moment of inertia is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> then the angular acceleration of the disc is:"}, "options": [{"id": "25ec7d", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a0"}, {"id": "2f32c3", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a1"}, {"id": "71b346", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a2"}, {"id": "29e334", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["6162faea6ed13040ec848e87"], "question": {"text": "A fly wheel is accelerated uniformly from rest and rotates through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>rad</mi></math> in the first second. The angle rotated by the fly wheel in the next second, will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "578d78", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a5"}, {"id": "9c52b9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a6"}, {"id": "b21443", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a7"}, {"id": "efa658", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6a9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "<p>A block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> slides with velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> on a frictionless horizontal surface and collides with a uniform vertical rod and sticks to it as shown. The rod is pivoted about&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and swings as a result of the collision making angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> before momentarily coming to rest. if the rod has mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is approximately<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>take</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8a20654d-618e-4fbf-b5f5-8ed1da4b332b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 232px; height: 149px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2ff61e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>63</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6aa"}, {"id": "583c22", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ab"}, {"id": "1be692", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>69</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ac"}, {"id": "caed68", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ad"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ae", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "<p>A sphere of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is rolling with an initial speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> goes up an inclined plane which makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the horizontal plane, without slipping. How low will the sphere take to return to the starting point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>?</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F43d3af2b-4789-4f83-b11d-6b2100a33ea2-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 321px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e6bcf5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6af"}, {"id": "bf6010", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>52</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b0"}, {"id": "6b862b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b1"}, {"id": "8a8418", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["6162faec6ed13040ec84909e"], "concepts": ["626bac5bc033d2244444961b"], "question": {"text": "A wheel is rolling on a plane surface. The speed of a particle on the highest point of the rim is $8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$. The speed of the particle on the rim of the wheel at the same level as the centre of wheel, will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "abdb72", "text": "$4 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b4"}, {"id": "765b65", "text": "$8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b5"}, {"id": "3bafae", "text": "$4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b6"}, {"id": "80a53e", "text": "$8 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b94a67dbe2603c3e992e"], "question": {"text": "Ratio of radius of gyration of a hollow sphere to that of a solid cylinder of equal mass, for moment of Inertia about their diameter axis $\\mathrm{AB}$ as shown in figure is $\\sqrt{8 / x}$. The value of $x$ is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FX2HVRwgsocDf1AWw9so1jfU3kfMh8eClEXm_MUQPg40.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "c45e48", "text": "$51$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6b9"}, {"id": "2ff2d9", "text": "$34$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ba"}, {"id": "e44849", "text": "$17$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6bb"}, {"id": "a6540b", "text": "$67$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6bc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6bd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ad"], "question": {"text": "<p>An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is hanging from one end of a uniform rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> pivoted at its end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> on a vertical wall as shown in figure. It is supported by a cable <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> such that the system is in equilibrium. The tension in the cable is:</p><p>(Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc5e79235-9257-4c5d-876a-5437ff397e19-9894007.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 397px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d2be0e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6be"}, {"id": "f0b43f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6bf"}, {"id": "0b69fb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c0"}, {"id": "b390db", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b55"], "question": {"text": "A body rolls down an inclined plane without slipping. The kinetic energy of rotation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its translational kinetic energy. The body is:"}, "options": [{"id": "bf449b", "text": "solid sphere", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c3"}, {"id": "7fdf78", "text": "solid cylinder", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c4"}, {"id": "c04cf7", "text": "hollow cylinder", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c5"}, {"id": "62ff7d", "text": "ring", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cad"], "question": {"text": "The time dependence of the position of a particle of mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is given by <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> . Its angular momentum, with respect to the origin, at time <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "366164", "text": "<math><mn>36</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c8"}, {"id": "921bc7", "text": "<math><mn>48</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6c9"}, {"id": "ca963c", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>48</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ca"}, {"id": "c43c8d", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6cb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6cc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["6162faec6ed13040ec84909e"], "concepts": ["6162faec6ed13040ec849082"], "question": {"text": "A solid spherical ball is rolling on a frictionless horizontal plane surface about its axis of symmetry. The ratio of rotational kinetic energy of the ball to its total kinetic energy is"}, "options": [{"id": "84dcd4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6cd"}, {"id": "bfa154", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6ce"}, {"id": "8704cb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6cf"}, {"id": "d00422", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473f"], "question": {"text": "A homogeneous solid cylindrical roller of radius <math><mi>R</mi></math> and mass <math><mi>M</mi></math> is pulled on a cricket pitch by a horizontal force. Assuming rolling without slipping, angular acceleration of the cylinder is:"}, "options": [{"id": "8cf99d", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi> </mi><mi>m</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d2"}, {"id": "c24a3b", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi> </mi><mi>m</mi><mi> </mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d3"}, {"id": "bf46fd", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi> </mi><mi>m</mi><mi> </mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d4"}, {"id": "34bb9c", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi> </mi><mi>m</mi><mi> </mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f6d6", "type": "singleC