 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3dc62f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f877"}, {"id": "3a4e24", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f878"}, {"id": "b25316", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f879"}, {"id": "fd7bbf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "The coordinates of a particle with respect to origin in a given reference frame is \\((1,1,1)\\) meters. If a force of \\(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}\\) acts on the particle, then the magnitude of torque (with respect to origin) in z-direction is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "4a5a9e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87c"}, {"id": "8e43ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87d"}, {"id": "c05822", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87e"}, {"id": "8ef2ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f87f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f880", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87cd"], "question": {"text": "The centre of a wheel rolling on a plane surface moves with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;A particle on the rim of the wheel at the same level as the centre will be moving at a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "e0a1ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f881"}, {"id": "fba968", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f882"}, {"id": "89b85c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f883"}, {"id": "4866d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f884"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925f885", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cad"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> moving with a uniform speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> plane along the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. The angular momentum of the particle about the origin will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3445a9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_